---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { links } from '../config';
// Imported raw so the wording is exactly what was written — nothing retyped.
import body from '../content/privacy.html?raw';

const contact = links.featureRequests;
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What Briefly knows about you, who else sees it, and how to get rid of it."
  body={body}
>
  <!-- The policy above is the app's, kept verbatim. This note covers the
       website itself, which the app policy does not. Keep it in step with
       worker/waitlist.js and the forms on the homepage. -->
  <section id="waitlist" class="site-note">
    <p class="site-note__label">This website</p>
    <h2>The waitlist and gro-usa.com</h2>
    <p>
      Everything above is about the Briefly app. This part is about this website, which is not the
      app and does not need an account.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>The waitlist.</strong> If you join, we keep your email address and nothing else.
        It is stored as a contact with Resend, the same company that sends the app's account
        emails. You get one confirmation straight away, and one more email when Briefly opens.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Feature requests.</strong> What you type is emailed to us at {contact}, sent
        through Resend, along with your email address if you chose to give one so we can reply.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>How it gets there.</strong> Both forms go through a small program we run on
        Cloudflare, which passes them to Resend. Cloudflare sees your IP address and uses it to
        limit how often the forms can be sent, so they cannot be used for spam. The site itself is
        hosted by GitHub Pages, which keeps ordinary server logs like any host.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Nothing else.</strong> No analytics, no cookies, no ads, no tracking, and the fonts
        are served from this site rather than from Google. After you join, your browser remembers
        that you did so the form does not ask again. That is a single flag on your device, not
        your email address, and it is never sent to us.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To come off the waitlist, email <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a> from the address
      you signed up with and we will delete it.
    </p>
  </section>
</Legal>

<style>
  /* Set apart from the policy above, so it reads as a separate note about the
     website rather than another clause of the app policy. */
  .site-note {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.5rem 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--paper-raised);
    scroll-margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .site-note__label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .site-note strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
</style>
